<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cuba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cuba is the largest island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, colonised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from the early sixteenth century. It remained one of the last colonies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> until 1898, with a plantation economy built on enslaved African labour. Many enslaved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> region were taken to Cuba, where their religion contributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santeria">Santería</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cuba.jpg" alt="Cuba" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miguel Teurbe Tolón and Narciso López · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cuba.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
